 fresh cursors, runs link-manifest synchronously for at most 64 drive rounds, and reports :pending . The :remote drive advances only a counter.'\n4 \"A dao.space.dht node's byte-store handle reads :local only. load-index stages a miss around the handle: walk against a probing handle, fetch the missing blob with :jing/get, walk again.\" \"A dao.space.dht node's byte-store handle reads :local only. load-index stages a miss around the handle: walk against a probing handle, fetch the missing blob with :jing/get , walk again.\"\n5 'src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:457-597; dao.jing.dht.md 5.1' 'src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:457-597 ; dao.jing.dht.md 5.1'\n6 \"The REPL's index holds AST datoms with :yin/address facts naming row addresses. The rows themselves are never stored: yin.vm/materialize-tree! has no caller in src/.\" \"The REPL's index holds AST datoms with :yin/address facts naming row addresses. The rows themselves are never stored: yin.vm/materialize-tree! has no caller in src/ .\"\n7 'src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1472' 'src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc ; src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1472'\n8 \"A REPL definition is the application (yin/def 'f value): operator the variable yin/def, first operand a literal symbol. Definitions are found by query; no definition-name fact exists.\" \"A REPL definition is the application (yin/def 'f value) : operator the variable yin/def , first operand a literal symbol. Definitions are found by query; no definition-name fact exists.\"\n9 'yin/vm.cljc:296; test/dao/space/query_test.cljc' 'yin/vm.cljc:296 ; test/dao/space/query_test.cljc'\n11 'linker.cljc:1992; test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:134' 'linker.cljc:1992 ; test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:134'\n13 'src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc; yin/repl.cljc:862' 'src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc ; yin/repl.cljc:862'\n17 'yin/repl.cljc:1848; yin/repl/main.cljc:286' 'yin/repl.cljc:1848 ; yin/repl/main.cljc:286'\n18 'The dao.space.dht host module answers load-index, load-status and q as effects on the query call pair, threading the node through query/serve.' 'The dao.space.dht host module answers load-index , load-status and q as effects on the query call pair, threading the node through query/serve .'\n21 'require_test.cljc:90-98; linker_test.cljc a-definition-dominating-every-application-discharges-a-body-occurrence; yin.vm.linker.md 4.2 step 5a' 'require_test.cljc:90-98 ; linker_test.cljc a-definition-dominating-every-application-discharges-a-body-occurrence ; yin.vm.linker.md 4.2 step 5a'\n24 'A DHT node holds at most 64 pending writes; a write beyond that is /busy.' 'A DHT node holds at most 64 pending writes; a write beyond that is /busy .'\n28 \"yin.vm/ast-requirements answers a tree's store keys (definitions included) and its effects, normalized by footprint-table. yin.vm/profile-of answers a primitive's profile with its :yin.k/effects.\" \"yin.vm/ast-requirements answers a tree's store keys (definitions included) and its effects, normalized by footprint-table . yin.vm/profile-of answers a primitive's profile with its :yin.k/effects .\"\n55 'The same name bound to the same address by several declared principals resolves, with every asserter in provenance. Different addresses refuse :ambiguous-name.' 'The same name bound to the same address by several declared principals resolves, with every asserter in provenance. Different addresses refuse :ambiguous-name .'\n75 'A blob that fails segment-matches?.' 'A blob that fails segment-matches? .'\n77 'manifest-defect.' 'manifest-defect .'\n79 'row-local-defect.' 'row-local-defect .'\n81 'record-defect.' 'record-defect .'\n87 \"An image that fails its format's :identity-matches-fn.\" \"An image that fails its format's :identity-matches-fn .\"\n95 'segment-matches?; manifest-defect is nil.' 'segment-matches? ; manifest-defect is nil.'\n98 \"A bounded worklist over the grammar's child slots (ast-format's :parts-fn); each row segment-matches? and has no row-local-defect.\" \"A bounded worklist over the grammar's child slots (ast-format's :parts-fn ); each row segment-matches? and has no row-local-defect .\"\n100 'The derivation record of each of :yin.semantic/code, :yin.debruijn.code, :yin.debruijn.register the manifest names' 'The derivation record of each of :yin.semantic/code , :yin.debruijn.code , :yin.debruijn.register the manifest names'\n101 'segment-matches?; record-defect is nil; :yin.ledger/input equals the tree.' 'segment-matches? ; record-defect is nil; :yin.ledger/input equals the tree.'\n104 \"Its storage address is the identity itself for the semantic vector, and the :yin.module/index entry for H and R; an identity with no index entry is :invalid. The image satisfies its format record's :identity-matches-fn.\" \"Its storage address is the identity itself for the semantic vector, and the :yin.module/index entry for H and R; an identity with no index entry is :invalid . The image satisfies its format record's :identity-matches-fn .\"\n111 \"No peer produced a. c is the /miss fact's reason for that address (/exhausted, /deadline, /solo, /busy), or :dao.jing.dht/gap when the fact was lost.\" \"No peer produced a . c is the /miss fact's reason for that address (/exhausted, /deadline , /solo , /busy ), or :dao.jing.dht/gap when the fact was lost.\"\n119 \"(yin.vm/ast-requirements db) over the $ast relation of the tree's rows, (vals (:rows (yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast))): its :store-keys, :effects, :ffi-ops and :parked-ids.\" \"(yin.vm/ast-requirements db) over the $ast relation of the tree's rows, (vals (:rows (yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast))) : its :store-keys , :effects , :ffi-ops and :parked-ids .\"\n121 \"Each declared profile's :yin.k/effects.\" \"Each declared profile's :yin.k/effects .\"\n123 'Each required manifest, read from handle: its own :yin.module/footprint :effects.' 'Each required manifest, read from handle : its own :yin.module/footprint :effects .'\n131 'The last outcome was not /sent. Carries that reason. May become sent by a later repair.' 'The last outcome was not /sent . Carries that reason. May become sent by a later repair.'\n148 'The first report: every blob has left waiting.' 'The first report: every blob has left waiting .'\n151 'After the first report, the :result changed (to :partial or to :acknowledged), whatever wrote the ledger, or repair ended. A change that ends repair is one event.' 'After the first report, the :result changed (to :partial or to :acknowledged ), whatever wrote the ledger, or repair ended. A change that ends repair is one event.'\n157 'Stays sent.' 'Stays sent .'\n159 'failed, nothing outstanding' 'failed , nothing outstanding'\n160 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled; the earlier reason is kept under :was.' 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled ; the earlier reason is kept under :was .'\n162 'waiting, queued' 'waiting , queued'\n163 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled.' 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled .'\n165 'waiting or failed, request outstanding' 'waiting or failed , request outstanding'\n166 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled.' 'failed with reason :dao.space.dht/cancelled .'\n175 '\"ed25519:\" + public.' '\"ed25519:\" + public .'\n180 '(key-text key), (key-from-text s)' '(key-text key) , (key-from-text s)'\n189 'A name both bind to the same manifest resolves (R8). A name they bind to different manifests is :ambiguous-name.' 'A name both bind to the same manifest resolves (R8). A name they bind to different manifests is :ambiguous-name .'\n201 ':name, :diagnostics for that name' ':name , :diagnostics for that name'\n202 \"The fold found no accepted assertion. Diagnostics name every discarded envelope for the name: :unauthenticated (:no-proof, :bad-proof), :undeclared-principal, :replay, :equivocation, :dangling-retraction (only when the retracted assertion is in the snapshot set), :malformed-envelope. A retraction of an assertion outside the set names no name. It is never here; it is reported once under the fold's :global-diagnostics (7.3).\" \"The fold found no accepted assertion. Diagnostics name every discarded envelope for the name: :unauthenticated (:no-proof, :bad-proof ), :undeclared-principal , :replay , :equivocation , :dangling-retraction (only when the retracted assertion is in the snapshot set), :malformed-envelope . A retraction of an assertion outside the set names no name. It is never here; it is reported once under the fold's :global-diagnostics (7.3).\"\n204 ':addresses, :asserters' ':addresses , :asserters'\n207 ':address, :cause the :miss cause' ':address , :cause the :miss cause'\n208 'The load failed :miss.' 'The load failed :miss .'\n211 \"The load failed :invalid: the closure walk's codes of 4.2, :dao.space.dht/walk-threw, or :dao.space.dht/walk-shape.\" \"The load failed :invalid : the closure walk's codes of 4.2, :dao.space.dht/walk-threw , or :dao.space.dht/walk-shape .\"\n213 \":address, :outcome the client's outcome keyword\" \":address , :outcome the client's outcome keyword\"\n214 'The load failed :unaskable.' 'The load failed :unaskable .'\n216 'the section 7.4 entry: :module, :name, :pinned, :binding, and its data' 'the section 7.4 entry: :module , :name , :pinned , :binding , and its data'\n223 ':contract-mismatch, :module-name-mismatch, :derivation-mismatch, :unverified-derivation, :undeclared-free, :use-before-definition, :unresolved-free, :shadowed-free, :unsupported-format, and the rest, unchanged.' ':contract-mismatch , :module-name-mismatch , :derivation-mismatch , :unverified-derivation , :undeclared-free , :use-before-definition , :unresolved-free , :shadowed-free , :unsupported-format , and the rest, unchanged.'\n224 ':yin.repl/abandoned, :yin.repl/link-policy' ':yin.repl/abandoned , :yin.repl/link-policy'\n232 'The walk (4.2) of a pinned manifest under :requires answers :invalid. Raised before anything is written.' 'The walk (4.2) of a pinned manifest under :requires answers :invalid . Raised before anything is written.'\n234 \":name, :walk the walk's :missing outcome\" \":name , :walk the walk's :missing outcome\"\n235 'A pinned manifest is present but its closure answers :missing beyond it. Raised before anything is written. A pinned manifest that is itself absent is /missing-requirement.' 'A pinned manifest is present but its closure answers :missing beyond it. Raised before anything is written. A pinned manifest that is itself absent is /missing-requirement .'\n238 'The walk of the closure just minted is not :complete. Raised after the writes and before any link: :links is never reported for it.' 'The walk of the closure just minted is not :complete . Raised after the writes and before any link: :links is never reported for it.'\n244 'No live publication of the manifest is repairing. Carries :manifest.' 'No live publication of the manifest is repairing. Carries :manifest .'\n247 'No live publication of the manifest. Carries :manifest.' 'No live publication of the manifest. Carries :manifest .'\n250 'The load record is :loading. Carries :address.' 'The load record is :loading . Carries :address .'\n253 'dao.space.dht/join, step, store, local, announce!, close!' 'dao.space.dht/join , step , store , local , announce! , close!'\n255 'dao.space.dht/load-index, load-status, db, q' 'dao.space.dht/load-index , load-status , db , q'\n257 'dao.space.dht/load, forget' 'dao.space.dht/load , forget'\n260 \"The covered-index manifests whose load is :loaded, sorted by address text. yin.vm.linker.dht/snapshots reads the node's loads only through it.\" \"The covered-index manifests whose load is :loaded , sorted by address text. yin.vm.linker.dht/snapshots reads the node's loads only through it.\"\n261 'dao.space.dht/retry!, cancel!' 'dao.space.dht/retry! , cancel!'\n264 'What the node retains now: {:fresh n :repair n :outstanding n :outstanding-fresh n :outstanding-repair n :live n :open n :repairing n :ledger-entries n}. These are queue entries, requests outstanding (in total and per queue), live publications, those awaiting a first report, those repairing, and the ledger entries live publications hold (section 5.5.2).' 'What the node retains now: {:fresh n :repair n :outstanding n :outstanding-fresh n :outstanding-repair n :live n :open n :repairing n :ledger-entries n} . These are queue entries, requests outstanding (in total and per queue), live publications, those awaiting a first report, those repairing, and the ledger entries live publications hold (section 5.5.2).'\n266 'Every live publication, oldest first, each {:manifest m :blobs n :sent s :result r :reported? b :repairing? b :delay ticks :due reading-or-nil :cycles n :cycle-open? b :repair-queued n :entries {address entry}}. An entry is {:state :waiting}, {:state :sent :peers k} or {:state :failed :reason r :peers k}, with :was after a cancellation.' 'Every live publication, oldest first, each {:manifest m :blobs n :sent s :result r :reported? b :repairing? b :delay ticks :due reading-or-nil :cycles n :cycle-open? b :repair-queued n :entries {address entry}} . An entry is {:state :waiting} , {:state :sent :peers k} or {:state :failed :reason r :peers k} , with :was after a cancellation.'\n270 'The distinct peers a blob must be handed to before it is sent.' 'The distinct peers a blob must be handed to before it is sent .'\n275 'yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!, footprint, module-from-index, assertion, retraction' 'yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module! , footprint , module-from-index , assertion , retraction'\n280 \"module-from-index over the publisher's own index db, publish!, and the envelopes of 6.6 signed with :key: {:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]}, the envelopes for the caller to commit as one index transaction before it announces; refused :yin.link.publish/no-key without a key. Every refusal writes nothing.\" \"module-from-index over the publisher's own index db , publish! , and the envelopes of 6.6 signed with :key : {:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]} , the envelopes for the caller to commit as one index transaction before it announces; refused :yin.link.publish/no-key without a key. Every refusal writes nothing.\"\n281 'yin.vm.linker.publish/next-seq, name-envelopes' 'yin.vm.linker.publish/next-seq , name-envelopes'\n292 \"The name's 7.3 entry when it resolves, else its section 9 refusal: :absent with :name and that name's :diagnostics, or :ambiguous-name with :name, :addresses, :asserters. The DHT link source refuses with it.\" \"The name's 7.3 entry when it resolves, else its section 9 refusal: :absent with :name and that name's :diagnostics , or :ambiguous-name with :name , :addresses , :asserters . The DHT link source refuses with it.\"\n298 'The section 9 row of a failed closure load, given the status module-status answers. :miss gives :absent with :cause. :invalid gives :descriptor-defect with :code, plus :detail and :text when present. :unaskable gives :yin.link.dht/unaskable with :outcome. It answers nil for a load that has not failed. The DHT link source refuses with this row, so there is one conversion, not two.' 'The section 9 row of a failed closure load, given the status module-status answers. :miss gives :absent with :cause . :invalid gives :descriptor-defect with :code , plus :detail and :text when present. :unaskable gives :yin.link.dht/unaskable with :outcome . It answers nil for a load that has not failed. The DHT link source refuses with this row, so there is one conversion, not two.'\n300 '7.4; refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded unless the load is :loaded.' '7.4; refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded unless the load is :loaded .'\n302 \"link-manifest over the node's local store; refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded unless the load is :loaded.\" \"link-manifest over the node's local store; refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded unless the load is :loaded .\"\n317 \"The fresh queue's capacity. Beyond: :dao.space.dht/backlog-full. Composition data to join.\" \"The fresh queue's capacity. Beyond: :dao.space.dht/backlog-full . Composition data to join .\"\n320 \"Most repair-queue entries one publication holds. The repair queue's own capacity is :max-repairing x :repair-batch.\" \"Most repair-queue entries one publication holds. The repair queue's own capacity is :max-repairing x :repair-batch .\"\n326 'Outstanding requests reserved for repair while its queue is non-empty. Below max-pending-writes.' 'Outstanding requests reserved for repair while its queue is non-empty. Below max-pending-writes .'\n335 'Beyond: the oldest is retired :dao.space.dht/displaced.' 'Beyond: the oldest is retired :dao.space.dht/displaced .'\n341 'yin.repl.link/attempt-budget, unchanged.' 'yin.repl.link/attempt-budget , unchanged.'\n347 \"Performance limit. names, resolve-name and dependency-bindings read <dir>/HEAD from disk and rebuild the HEAD index's datoms on every fold, and every name a require resolves folds once. Resolution cost therefore grows with the publisher's own index size. No cache is kept; one is admissible only if invalidated on every HEAD change and every index load.\" \"Performance limit. names , resolve-name and dependency-bindings read <dir>/HEAD from disk and rebuild the HEAD index's datoms on every fold, and every name a require resolves folds once. Resolution cost therefore grows with the publisher's own index size. No cache is kept; one is admissible only if invalidated on every HEAD change and every index load.\"\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md 113 113 cells equal: False\n19 'Contacts [{:host ip-literal :port p} ...]: unproven candidates, nothing more.' 'Contacts [{:host ip-literal :port p} ...] : unproven candidates, nothing more.'\n32 '/address, /peers n' '/address , /peers n'\n33 'The acknowledgement. Every datagram of the write was handed to the socket toward n distinct peers, n >= ack-peers.' 'The acknowledgement. Every datagram of the write was handed to the socket toward n distinct peers, n >= ack-peers .'\n35 '/address, /reason, /peers m, /local' '/address , /reason , /peers m , /local'\n36 'The write is not acknowledged. m < ack-peers is how many peers it was sent to; /local is the local verdict or nil.' 'The write is not acknowledged. m < ack-peers is how many peers it was sent to; /local is the local verdict or nil .'\n38 '/address, /peers n, /confirmed c' '/address , /peers n , /confirmed c'\n41 '/address, /reason' '/address , /reason'\n42 'A get ended not found: /exhausted, /deadline, /solo, /busy.' 'A get ended not found: /exhausted , /deadline , /solo , /busy .'\n56 'The encoded store message exceeds max-message-bytes. Answered at once.' 'The encoded store message exceeds max-message-bytes . Answered at once.'\n72 'Floor 2, ceiling k.' 'Floor 2, ceiling k .'\n79 ':dao.jing.dht/query-ticks, /tries' ':dao.jing.dht/query-ticks , /tries'\n88 ':dao.jing.dht/max-pending-writes, /max-pending-gets' ':dao.jing.dht/max-pending-writes , /max-pending-gets'\n90 'Beyond: /busy, or not found with a /miss.' 'Beyond: /busy , or not found with a /miss .'\n99 \"The socket's :max-bytes.\" \"The socket's :max-bytes .\"\n105 'dao.jing.dht/IDhtNet, lookup, create-content-dht (a waiting transport protocol; put replicates and get fetches synchronously)' 'dao.jing.dht/IDhtNet , lookup , create-content-dht (a waiting transport protocol; put replicates and get fetches synchronously)'\n106 \"Deleted in S3, together with dao.jing.dht.node, which implements and calls them (Architect ruling on the S2 sign-off). S2's core does not use them.\" \"Deleted in S3, together with dao.jing.dht.node , which implements and calls them (Architect ruling on the S2 sign-off). S2's core does not use them.\"\n107 'dao.jing.dht.node (create-node, create-content-dht-udp; JVM only, own DatagramSocket and receiver thread, one Transit-JSON map per datagram, node id sha256(host:port), claimed :from observed unvalidated, replies matched by id alone, oversize dropped silently)' 'dao.jing.dht.node (create-node, create-content-dht-udp ; JVM only, own DatagramSo